**The bug:** the semicolon right after the `for(...)` header. That `;` makes the loop body empty, so the loop runs 10 times doing nothing, and the `{ }` block ends up outside the loop — where `i` is out of scope, causing the compile error (`'i' was not declared in this scope`).

**Fixed code — just delete the semicolon:**

```cpp
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    cout << i;
}
```

This prints `0123456789`. If you need them separated, use `cout << i << " ";` instead.

(If it still won't compile, make sure `#include <iostream>` and `using namespace std;` are at the top.)
